 "summary": "The kernel subspace, the constancy theorem and the dimension results are new for real-differentiable functions; they reuse Mathlib's `MDifferentiable.exists_eq_const_of_compactSpace`, `LinearMap.const`, `Function.const_injective` and `LinearEquiv.ofInjective`, which fixes the prior finding. Related results already in Tau Ceti (`delBar_eq_zero_iff_exists_eq_const_of_compactSpace`, `holomorphicEquivOfCompactSpace`, `zeroZeroEquivOfCompactSpace`) cover only smooth forms or holomorphic maps, so none of them replaces this material.",
